  "hindi": "वही जन के साथ, वही कुल के साथ, वही जन्म से, वही पुत्रों के साथ पुरस्कार और धन मनुष्यों के साथ ले जाता है; जो श्रद्धापूर्ण मन वाला होकर देवों के पिता ब्रह्मणस्पति की हवि द्वारा सेवा करता है।",
  "english": "He indeed, with the people, with the clan, by birth, with sons, carries off the prize and wealth with men; he who, faithful-minded, honours with an oblation the father of the gods, Brahmaṇaspati.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "śraddhāmanā is taken as an instrumental form agreeing loosely with haviṣā ('faithful-minded'); it may instead refer to the worshipper. 'father of the gods' is the text's own apposition. śraddhāmanā is read as nom. sg. śraddhā-manāḥ agreeing with yaḥ (visarga lost before h).",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "type": "verse",
  "line_ids": [
   "002.026.3a",
   "002.026.3b"
  ],
  "lines_deva": [
   "स इज्जने॑न॒ स वि॒शा स जन्म॑ना॒ स पु॒त्रैर्वाजं॑ भरते॒ धना॒ नृभि॑:",
   "दे॒वानां॒ यः पि॒तर॑मा॒विवा॑सति श्र॒द्धाम॑ना ह॒विषा॒ ब्रह्म॑ण॒स्पति॑म्"
  ],
  "lines_iast": [
